    "active": true,
    "description": "<p><strong>CLASS TYPE</strong> Martial</p>\n<p>For you, martial skill transcends the battlefield it is a lifestyle, a doctrine, and a state of mind. You search out methods of battle beyond swords and shields, finding weapons within themselves just as capable of crippling or killing as any blade. You elevate your body to become a weapon of war, from battle-minded ascetic to self-taught brawler. You tread the path of discipline, to discover within yourself not what you are, but what you are meant to be.</p>\n<p>You excel at overcoming even the most daunting perils, striking where it’s least expected, and taking advantage of enemy vulnerabilities. Fleet of foot and skilled in combat, you can navigate any battlefield with ease, aiding allies wherever you are needed most.</p>\n<p><strong>MAGICAL TRADITION</strong> You do not gain a normal spellcasting progression. Your Monastic Path determines the magical tradition and magical ability score of any innate spells or magical techniques you gain from Disciple abilities or feats.</p>",
    "classType": "Martial",
    "keyAbilityScores": "Wisdom (min +2), Dexterity, Strength",
    "classSkills": "Acrobatics, Artistry, Athletics, Climbing, Culture, Meditation, Mental Focus, Perception, Sense Motive, Stealth",
    "grantedFeats": "1: Inner Discipline",
    "classAbilities": "1: Powerful Fists, 1: Disciple's Dodge, 1: Disciple's Resolve, 1: Flurry of Blows, 1: Deep Focus, 1: Monastic Path, 4: Incredible Movement",
    "proficiencies": "You may use all simple weapons and any weapons that have the monastic trait (see chapter 6).",
